  "label": "Liberals are mapped onto Sheldon Cooper",
  "description": "The top text 'why are liberals so angry?' is mapped onto the visual of Jim Parsons as Sheldon Cooper. The meme uses Sheldon's sarcastic and annoyed expression to visually represent the stereotype that liberals are 'angry,' implying that the character (and by extension, the group he represents) is the source of the anger being questioned. This is an analogical mapping where the textual entity 'liberals' is projected onto the visual entity 'Sheldon Cooper' through the character's demeanor.",
